
Install ffmpeg
• Go to the official FFmpeg Download Page and choose a Windows build (such as builds by BtbN or gyan.dev).
   https://github.com/BtbN/FFmpeg-Builds/releases
• Extract the downloaded archive and move the folder to C:\ffmpeg.
• Open Windows search, type Environment Variables, and select Edit the system environment variables.
• Click Environment Variables, select the Path variable under system or user variables, and click Edit.
• Add the full path to the bin folder (e.g., C:\ffmpeg\bin) and save all dialog boxes.
